# Post-GUI HAL file of the G0759 under CoffeeCNC: [HAL] POSTGUI_HALFILE of G0759-coffeecnc.ini.
# coffeecnc runs it once its HAL component 'coffeecnc' exists. It takes the place of
# postgui_call_list.hal and custom_postgui.hal, which connect gmoccapy pins and cannot load
# without gmoccapy; neither is read under CoffeeCNC. rpm.hal (the embedded rpm.glade meter of
# gmoccapy) is not loaded either.
#
# Module loads: G0759.hal and custom.hal load trivkins, motmod, hostmot2, hm2_eth, pid, near,
# scale, abs, not and limit1. Neither watchdog nor lut5 is among them, so both load here. A file
# added to [HAL] HALFILE later that loads one of them must take these instances into its own
# loadrt line, and the two loadrt lines here must go.
# Nothing in G0759.hal or custom.hal connects motion.jog-stop, motion.jog-inhibit,
# iocontrol.0.tool-change, tool-changed or tool-prep-number: each gets its only connection here.

# ---- CoffeeCNC's own fragment: the commands of share/coffeecnc/hal/coffeecnc_postgui.hal of
# ---- CoffeeCNC 0.1.0, in its order and unchanged. The thread is this machine's servo-thread.

# Jog stop without the NML command channel. motion.jog-stop aborts every jog in motion while it
# is high; motion.jog-inhibit refuses a jog before it starts. Both are high while coffeecnc asks
# for a stop (coffeecnc.jog-stop), or the watchdog has tripped because coffeecnc.heartbeat
# stopped toggling: the program died or stalled.
loadrt watchdog num_inputs=1
loadrt lut5 names=coffeecnc-jog-stop,coffeecnc-jog-inhibit
addf watchdog.process servo-thread
addf watchdog.set-timeouts servo-thread
addf coffeecnc-jog-stop servo-thread
addf coffeecnc-jog-inhibit servo-thread

setp watchdog.timeout-0 0.3
setp coffeecnc-jog-stop.function 0xD
setp coffeecnc-jog-inhibit.function 0xD
net coffeecnc-heartbeat coffeecnc.heartbeat => watchdog.input-0
net coffeecnc-watchdog-enable coffeecnc.watchdog-enable => watchdog.enable-in
net coffeecnc-watchdog-ok watchdog.ok-out => coffeecnc.watchdog-ok
net coffeecnc-watchdog-ok => coffeecnc-jog-stop.in-0 coffeecnc-jog-inhibit.in-0
net coffeecnc-jog-stop-request coffeecnc.jog-stop => coffeecnc-jog-stop.in-1
net coffeecnc-jog-stop-request => coffeecnc-jog-inhibit.in-1
net coffeecnc-jog-stop coffeecnc-jog-stop.out => motion.jog-stop
net coffeecnc-jog-inhibit coffeecnc-jog-inhibit.out => motion.jog-inhibit

# Manual tool change: coffeecnc asks the operator and answers iocontrol itself. No
# hal_manualtoolchange is loaded. The two unlinkp lines do nothing on this machine (the pins are
# not connected before this file runs); they are the fragment's.
unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-change
unlinkp iocontrol.0.tool-changed
net coffeecnc-tool-change iocontrol.0.tool-change => coffeecnc.tool-change
net coffeecnc-tool-number iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number => coffeecnc.tool-number
net coffeecnc-tool-changed coffeecnc.tool-changed => iocontrol.0.tool-changed

# ---- This machine.

# From custom_postgui.hal: a prepared tool needs no action.
net tool-prep-loop iocontrol.0.tool-prepare => iocontrol.0.tool-prepared

# Signals of G0759.hal, declared in [COFFEECNC] of the INI file. Each already has its writer
# there; coffeecnc only reads.
net spindle-vel-fb-rpm-abs => coffeecnc.spindle-rpm
net spindle-at-speed => coffeecnc.spindle-at-speed
net probe-in => coffeecnc.probe-input
